      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I have the answer directly from the wiki.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there at all**. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes** \u2014 specifically into the Ingest agent and Query agent \u2014 immediately before those processes start\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its environment variables, since the key only exists inside the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API.",
